        {
          "stepNumber": 1,
          "part": null,
          "description": "Forming and solving equations for the Arithmetic Progression",
          "studentWork": "Let the speed of the train be x km/h. Reduced speed = (x − 8) km/h.\nTime at usual speed = 480/x, time at reduced speed = 480/(x − 8).\n480/x − 480/(x − 8) = 3\n⇒ 480(x − 8) − 480x = 3x(x − 8)\n⇒ −3840 = 3x² − 24x\n⇒ 3x² − 24x + 3840 = 0\n⇒ x² − 8x + 1280 = 0\n⇒ (x − 40)(x + 32) = 0\n⇒ x = 40 or x = −32. Speed cannot be negative.\n∴ Speed of the train = 40 km/h.",
          "status": "incorrect",
          "marksAvailable": 5.0,
          "marksAwarded": 0,
          "marksDeducted": 5.0,
          "teacherAnnotation": "× Completely different question answered (speed-distance problem instead of the given AP question).",
          "mistakeType": "conceptual",
          "correctedWorking": "Let first term = a, common difference = d. Given a + a_8 = 32 ⇒ a + (a + 7d) = 32 ⇒ 2a + 7d = 32, so a_8 = 32 - a. Also a · a_8 = 60 ⇒ a(32 - a) = 60 ⇒ a² - 32a + 60 = 0 ⇒ (a - 30)(a - 2) = 0. If a = 2, a_8 = 30 ⇒ 7d = 28 ⇒ d = 4. Then S_20 = (20/2)[2(2) + 19(4)] = 10[4 + 76] = 800. If a = 30, a_8 = 2 ⇒ 7d = -28 ⇒ d = -4. Then S_20 = (20/2)[2(30) + 19(-4)] = 10[60 - 76] = -160.",
          "isDeparture": true,
          "departureKind": "different-problem",
          "isReturn": false
        }
      ],
      "mistakeSummary": {
        "conceptual": 1,
        "calculation": 0,
        "silly": 0,
        "presentation": 0
      },
      "studentFinalAnswer": "∴ Speed of the train = 40 km/h.",
      "finalAnswerCorrect": false,
      "teacherNote": "You have answered an entirely different question involving train speeds and quadratic equations instead of the set Arithmetic Progression problem. Please ensure you carefully match your solution to the question asked."
    }
  ],
